{"type":"text","timestamp":1790445869236,"sessionID":"ses_f2120ad6bffe6a18JIcWBSPx65","part":{"id":"prt_0dee3d89a001Yc1U00t32sw4kR","messageID":"msg_0dee3a43b0015PazLJdXahx1UW","sessionID":"ses_f2120ad6bffe6a18JIcWBSPx65","type":"text","text":"The task is complete. Here's a summary of the changes made to `/workspace/scripts/steer_component.gd`:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**1. Capture debug data in `steer()`** — whenever `debug_enabled` is true, the script now stores the three steering vectors into the `debug` dictionary via `update_debug()`:\n\n```gdscript\nvar steering_adjustment := (scaled_desired_velocity - velocity) / mass\nif debug_enabled:\n    update_debug({\n        \"velocity\": velocity,\n        \"scaled_desired_velocity\": scaled_desired_velocity,\n        \"steering_force\": steering_adjustment,\n    })\nreturn velocity + steering_adjustment\n```\n\n**2. Queue a redraw every frame in `_process()`** — so the debug overlay can update continuously:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n    if debug_enabled:\n        queue_redraw()\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- ✅ Script passes Godot's parse check (`--check-only`, exit code 0)\n- ✅ Project runs headless for 30 frames with no errors (exit code 0)\n- ✅ Ran the game in Movie Maker mode — the fish sprite renders and moves toward the mouse (frame captures confirm steering behavior is working, with the `SteerComponent` active and `debug_enabled = true` set by `fish.gd`)\n\nThe debug dictionary now buffers the current velocity, scaled desired velocity, and steering force each time `steer()` runs (matching the pattern from Cashew OldDew's steering debug vectors tutorial), and `queue_redraw()` is called every frame while debugging is enabled so the overlay stays up to date.","time":{"start":1790445869210,"end":1790445869213},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_ce5a831dec5e4e64b317eee060bbb5a4_msg"}}}}
